---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import PlanCard from "../components/PlanCard.astro";
import {
	CONTACT_EMAIL,
	PLANS,
	PULSE_BASE,
	SHARED_FEATURES,
	SITE_TITLE,
	X_HANDLE,
	X_URL,
} from "../consts";

const title = `Pricing — ${SITE_TITLE}`;
const description =
	"NanoPulse pricing: 5 monitors free, 50 for $9/month, 500 for $29/month. Unlimited pings and Slack alerts on every plan.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">NanoPulse pricing</p>
				<h1>You pay for monitors. Everything else is included.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					A monitor is one thing you want to hear about: a nightly backup, a queue worker, a
					certificate renewal. Pings are unlimited on every plan, because charging per heartbeat
					would just teach you to ping less.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="plans">
				{PLANS.map((plan) => <PlanCard plan={plan} />)}
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>In every plan, including the free one</h2>
				<ul class="shared">
					{SHARED_FEATURES.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>Questions you would reasonably ask</h2>

				<div class="qa">
					<h3>How do I get a key, and how do I pay?</h3>
					<p>
						Mail <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> — or ping
						<a href={X_URL} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{X_HANDLE}</a> on X — and you get a key
						the same day, with an invoice to follow for the paid plans. Provisioning is deliberately
						manual while the service is young: a human reads every request, and there is no card
						form to trust. Self-serve checkout comes when the volume justifies it.
					</p>

					<h3>What happens when I hit my monitor limit?</h3>
					<p>
						Creating the next monitor is refused with a clear error. Pings to monitors that already
						exist are <strong>never</strong> rejected for quota reasons — a billing question must
						never be able to switch off your monitoring. Delete a monitor and the slot is free
						immediately.
					</p>

					<h3>Can I change plan later?</h3>
					<p>
						Yes, and it takes effect instantly: a plan here is just a number on your account, so
						there is no migration and nothing to re-create.
					</p>

					<h3>How fast will I know?</h3>
					<p>
						A scheduled sweep runs every minute, so an alert lands between zero and 60 seconds
						after your interval plus grace period has passed. If you need second-level
						precision, say so — that is a different product and I would rather tell you than sell
						you this one.
					</p>

					<h3>Where do alerts go?</h3>
					<p>
						To any HTTPS webhook. The body is Slack-shaped (<code>text</code> at the top level), so a
						Slack incoming webhook works with no configuration, and anything else gets structured
						JSON in the same request. Email and SMS alerts are not built.
					</p>

					<h3>Is there an API for everything?</h3>
					<p>
						There is only an API. Create and update monitors, read ping and event history, rotate and
						revoke your own keys — all under <code>{PULSE_BASE}/v1</code>. There is no dashboard to
						learn, and that is on purpose.
					</p>

					<h3>What if the service itself goes down?</h3>
					<p>
						Then you are not monitored, and honesty is the only answer available: there is no SLA on
						the free plan, and no promise I cannot keep on the paid ones. It runs on Cloudflare's
						edge with a serverless database, which is a good bet, not a guarantee. For
						life-critical monitoring, use two independent providers.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="closing card">
				<h2>Start on the free plan</h2>
				<p>Five monitors, unlimited pings, Slack alerts. Upgrade the day you need the sixth.</p>
				<a class="button" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=NanoPulse%20API%20key`}>Get an API key</a>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.intro {
		padding: 2em 0 0;
		max-width: 40em;
	}
	.lede {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
	}
	.plans {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		gap: 1.1em;
		margin: 2.5em 0 0;
	}
	.band {
		padding: 3em 0 0;
	}
	ul.shared {
		list-style: none;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		gap: 0.6em 1.5em;
		margin: 1.2em 0 0;
		padding: 0;
	}
	ul.shared li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 1.6em;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	ul.shared li::before {
		content: "✓";
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--alive);
	}
	.qa {
		max-width: 44em;
	}
	.qa h3 {
		margin-top: 1.6em;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}
	.qa p {
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.closing {
		margin-top: 3.5em;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.closing p {
		color: var(--muted);
		margin-bottom: 1.4em;
	}
	@media (max-width: 980px) {
		.plans {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 620px) {
		.plans,
		ul.shared {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
